entries.content:
• rejoice in the Lord: This theme appears again in Philippians 4:4 (see also Philippians 1:18; Philippians 2:17–18, Philippians 2:28; Philippians 4:10). 

• the same things: The meaning here is unclear. It might refer to:

• the recent encouragement to rejoice in the Lord;

• the earlier advice to follow Christ’s example (Philippians 2:1–18);

• Paul’s encouragement in general; or

• the upcoming warning about threats to their faith.
